meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still
==============================

Seamless still logo for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK. U-Boot shows a logo shortly
after power-on. The kernel takes over the running display instead of resetting
it. The logo stays on screen until Weston draws its first frame.

Tested with RZ/G3L BSP v1.0.0, MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l", core-image-weston.


I. Changes
==========

  U-Boot    A display driver brings up HDMI and shows the logo from /boot
            (1280x720).
  Kernel    The logo memory is reserved. The display drivers take over the
            running display. The framebuffer console and fbdev emulation are
            disabled.
  Image     The logo files are installed into /boot: the Renesas wordmark,
            white on Renesas blue, rendered at 1280x720 and 1920x1080.


II. Build
=========

Start from the default BSP build environment (RZ/G3L Linux Start-up Guide,
2.2) and add the layer:

  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still

Build:

  $ MACHINE=smarc-rzg3l bitbake core-image-weston


III. Notes
==========

  - Cannot be combined with meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-sequence.
  - With meta-rzg3l-fast-boot: add meta-rzg3l-fast-boot first.
    Both layers patch the same device tree file, in bblayers.conf order.
  - The logo files are gzip-compressed raw ARGB8888 frame buffers, in
    recipes-graphics/rzg3l-seamless-logo-still-image/files. To change the
    resolution, DISPLAY_MODE in U-Boot patch 0002 and
    renesas,seamless-boot-logo-vic in kernel patch 0008 must match
    (MIPI_DSI_720P: 4, MIPI_DSI_1080P: 16).
